{"text": "CONFIDENTIAL\n\nINTER:OFFICE CORRESPONDENCE\n\nPHILIP MORRIS U.S. A.\n\nRichmond, Virginia\n\nTo: -J. DeBlasio pate\n\n: November 10, 1989\nFrom: .B. Kanipe\n\nSubject: .Discolored Orifice Cups\n\nAfter extensive analytical evaluation of the discolored orifice cups,\nwe have been unable to determine the source of discoloration.\u2019 Conse-\nquently, all batches/lots containing such discolored orifice cups are\nreleased only for use in machinery testing at the Machinery Development\nCenter. Should this problem recur in future batches of orifice cups or any\nother cups produced by EFI, please notify us immediately so we may obtain\nthe necessary samples (e.g., water, cleaning solution, ete.) to pinpoint the\ncause for discoloration.\n\nIf you have any further questions regarding this matter, please let me\n\nknow.\n\n* Memo from B. Kanipe to D. Leyden, \u201cAnalytical Evaluation of Discolored\nOrifice Cups,\" November 10, 1989.\n\nR. Alley\nJ. Charles\nGrantham\n\nco Bucky Lan eps\n\nC89-07707\n\nHuon\n\nO89Z9Tzz0z",
